# Prisma checksums each applied migration by the bytes of its migration.sql and
# refuses to run when one no longer matches what was recorded. With
# core.autocrlf=true and no rule here, a plain checkout rewrites LF to CRLF and
# every already-applied migration "changes" - which is what happened: four
# migrations were recorded with LF and later checked out as CRLF, and
# `prisma migrate dev` then offered to reset the database over it.
#
# Pinning LF makes the working-tree bytes stable across machines and checkouts.
# Scoped to migrations rather than the whole repo: these are the only files
# whose exact bytes are load-bearing.
prisma/migrations/**/*.sql text eol=lf
